<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex1Xf.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{TableName:Datatype}^{\lx@paragraphsign}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖺𝖻𝗅𝖾𝖭𝖺𝗆𝖾</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>𝖣𝖺𝗍𝖺𝗍𝗒𝗉𝖾</mi><mi>¶</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{TableName:Datatype}^{\lx@paragraphsign}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S4.F2.fig1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><sup id="S4.F2.fig1.2.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.F2.fig1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">†</span></sup><span id="S4.F2.fig1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Table schema: includes table names, column names, column datatypes, and any constraints.</span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S4.F2.fig1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><sup id="S4.F2.fig1.3.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.F2.fig1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">‡</span></sup><span id="S4.F2.fig1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> SQL query that may contain placeholders, where <math id="S4.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Table}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖺𝖻𝗅𝖾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Table}</annotation></semantics></math> placeholders can be located in the <span id="S4.F2.fig1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FROM</span> clause and subqueries, while <math id="S4.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Expression}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤𝗑𝗉𝗋𝖾𝗌𝗌𝗂𝗈𝗇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Expression}</annotation></semantics></math> placeholders can be located anywhere an expression is allowed within the scope of its associated table name.</span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S4.F2.fig1.4" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><sup id="S4.F2.fig1.4.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.F2.fig1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">§</span></sup><span id="S4.F2.fig1.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> A placeholder that must be instantiated with a subquery returning a table whose column names and datatypes match the specification.</span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S4.F2.fig1.5" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><sup id="S4.F2.fig1.5.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.F2.fig1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">¶</span></sup><span id="S4.F2.fig1.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> A placeholder that must be instantiated with a concrete SQL expression which returns the specified datatype from the specified table in <math id="S4.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Schema}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝖼𝗁𝖾𝗆𝖺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Schema}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2. </span>BNF Grammar for CAQ Pairs, where we omit the full SQL grammar for simplicity.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we formally introduce <em id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Constrained Abstract Query (CAQ)</em>, the core concept of <span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">Argus</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A CAQ is a SQL query template that contains placeholders to be instantiated with concrete SQL snippets, along with constraints that specify valid instantiations for each placeholder.
<a href="#S4.F2.fig1" title="In 4. Constrained Abstract Query ‣ Automated Discovery of Test Oracles for Database Management Systems Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents the BNF grammar for CAQ pairs, which consists of two CAQs and their shared associated schema.
Each CAQ contains a SQL query with placeholders and a mapping that specifies the constraints for instantiating each placeholder.
A placeholder can be constrained to be instantiated with either an <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Expression}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤𝗑𝗉𝗋𝖾𝗌𝗌𝗂𝗈𝗇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Expression}</annotation></semantics></math> or a <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Table}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖺𝖻𝗅𝖾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Table}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The key motivation behind the two types of placeholder design is to use <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Expression}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤𝗑𝗉𝗋𝖾𝗌𝗌𝗂𝗈𝗇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Expression}</annotation></semantics></math> to cover most functions and operators-related features, and use <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Table}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖺𝖻𝗅𝖾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Table}</annotation></semantics></math> to cover features that require subqueries and clauses, such as <span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">JOIN</span>, <span id="S4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">EXISTS</span>, and <span id="S4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IN</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, an expression placeholder specifies the table name and the expected return datatype of the expression, such as <span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BOOLEAN</span>, <span id="S4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">INT</span>, and <span id="S4.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TEXT</span>.
A table placeholder specifies the expected schema of the table returned by the subquery, including column names and datatypes.
Note that, <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Table}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖺𝖻𝗅𝖾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Table}</annotation></semantics></math> can be located anywhere in the query where a SQL table is allowed, such as the <span id="S4.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FROM</span> clause and subqueries.
Meanwhile, <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Expression}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤𝗑𝗉𝗋𝖾𝗌𝗌𝗂𝗈𝗇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Expression}</annotation></semantics></math> can be located anywhere an expression with its specific datatype is allowed within the scope of its associated table name.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We then define how we instantiate a CAQ and the equivalence between a CAQ pair by extending the definitions in  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2017</a>)</cite> to our context.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Definition 4.1 (CAQ Instantiation).</h6>
<div id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{CAQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖢𝖠𝖰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{CAQ}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and its <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{PlaceholderMap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖯𝗅𝖺𝖼𝖾𝗁𝗈𝗅𝖽𝖾𝗋𝖬𝖺𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{PlaceholderMap}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\square_{1}\mapsto c_{1},\square_{2}\mapsto c_{2},\ldots,\square_{k}\mapsto c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\square_{1}\mapsto c_{1},\square_{2}\mapsto c_{2},\ldots,\square_{k}\mapsto c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, an <span id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">instantiation</span> of <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, is obtained by replacing each placeholder <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> with a concrete SQL snippet <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies the corresponding constraint <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and a set of general constraints <math id="S4.Thmlemma1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. The substitution can be written as:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q^{*}=q[\square_{1}\leftarrow s_{1},\square_{2}\leftarrow s_{2},\ldots,\square_{k}\leftarrow s_{k}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}=q[\square_{1}\leftarrow s_{1},\square_{2}\leftarrow s_{2},\ldots,\square_{k}\leftarrow s_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, each <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the <span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">Type</span> constraints shown in <a href="#S4.F2.fig1" title="In 4. Constrained Abstract Query ‣ Automated Discovery of Test Oracles for Database Management Systems Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
In addition, to prevent false positive bug reports when using the instantiated query <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for testing, we must also satisfy a set of general constraints <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, such as avoiding non-deterministic features, <em id="S4.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</em> <span id="S4.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RANDOM</span> and <span id="S4.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CURRENT_TIMESTAMP</span>, and ensuring the snippet is valid SQL.
Note that these are also widely adopted constraints in prior work on manually designed test oracles <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rigger and Su, 2020b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang and Su, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang and Rigger, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ba and Rigger, 2023</a>)</cite>.
The details about <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> can be found in <a href="#S6.SS2" title="6.2. Query Instantiation ‣ 6. Test Cases Instantiation ‣ Automated Discovery of Test Oracles for Database Management Systems Using LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We say that two CAQs are equivalent if all their possible instantiations are semantically equivalent.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Definition 4.2 (Equivalent CAQ Pair).</h6>
<div id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given two <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{CAQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖢𝖠𝖰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{CAQ}</annotation></semantics></math>s <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> defined over the same <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Schema}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝖼𝗁𝖾𝗆𝖺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Schema}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> (which specifies the tables referenced in both queries) with the same <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{PlaceholderMap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖯𝗅𝖺𝖼𝖾𝗁𝗈𝗅𝖽𝖾𝗋𝖬𝖺𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{PlaceholderMap}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\square_{1}\mapsto c_{1},\square_{2}\mapsto c_{2},\ldots,\square_{k}\mapsto c_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\square_{1}\mapsto c_{1},\square_{2}\mapsto c_{2},\ldots,\square_{k}\mapsto c_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> form an <span id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Equivalent CAQ Pair</span>, denoted <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,q_{1},q_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,q_{1},q_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, if for every possible instantiated concrete queries <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{2}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{2}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}^{*}\equiv q_{2}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}^{*}\equiv q_{2}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., they will return the same result set when executed on any database instance conforming to schema <math id="S4.Thmlemma2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">According to the above definition, once we verify that two CAQs form an equivalent pair, we can derive multiple concrete equivalent SQL query pairs by instantiating the CAQs with various snippets that satisfy the constraints of the placeholders.
Therefore, we transformed the test oracle discovery problem to the CAQ pair generation and equivalence checking problems.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Test Oracle Discovery</h2>

<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span><math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TestOracleDiscovery}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝖳𝖾𝗌𝗍𝖮𝗋𝖺𝖼𝗅𝖾𝖣𝗂𝗌𝖼𝗈𝗏𝖾𝗋𝗒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TestOracleDiscovery}</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span><span id="algorithm1.4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
A DBMS <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, an LLM <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, a prover <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, a grammar-based generator <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of schemas <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of maximum trials for each seed query <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{MaxDepth}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬𝖺𝗑𝖣𝖾𝗉𝗍𝗁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{MaxDepth}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><span id="algorithm1.4.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">A set of test oracles </span><math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.4.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Function</span><span id="algorithm1.4.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><em id="algorithm1.4.3.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;"><math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GenerateEqual}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖦𝖾𝗇𝖾𝗋𝖺𝗍𝖾𝖤𝗊𝗎𝖺𝗅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GenerateEqual}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.4.3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_upright">(<em id="algorithm1.4.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_serif ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M},\mathcal{D},\mathcal{P},q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M},\mathcal{D},\mathcal{P},q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{StopThreshold}\leftarrow 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖲𝗍𝗈𝗉𝖳𝗁𝗋𝖾𝗌𝗁𝗈𝗅𝖽</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{StopThreshold}\leftarrow 3</annotation></semantics></math></em>)</span></em><span id="algorithm1.4.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">:</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">2</span></span>
