</section>
<section id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Examples (3)</h4>

<div id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Listing <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> shows another bug in Dolt with the handling of <span id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LATERAL</span> joins in Dolt, which was detected using an oracle that leverages the semantics of <span id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CROSS JOIN</span> and <span id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LATERAL</span> joins.
Specifically, if a <span id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CROSS JOIN LATERAL</span> is used to join a left table with a static right table, <em id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</em> a <math id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Table}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳𝖺𝖻𝗅𝖾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Table}</annotation></semantics></math> placeholder <math id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the result should be identical to a regular <span id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CROSS JOIN</span> with the same right table, <em id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.,</em> the first query is semantically equivalent to the second query.
However, due to a bug in Dolt’s handling of <span id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LATERAL</span> joins, when instantiating the right table to <span id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(SELECT 1 AS c0) AS v</span>, the first query incorrectly returns an empty result set instead of the expected row.</p>
</div>
